+- J02 / local: Player pauses, opens settings, returns, resumes and immediately steers without a focus/input surprise
+- J03 / local: Player completes a three-race cup, reloads between rounds, and keeps exactly one set of rewards
+- J04 / local: Player completes all twelve events with ordinary inputs/resources and sees the held final scene
+- J05 / local: Player compares and equips a part, tests it and can explain its tradeoff
+- J06 / local: Player finishes a Time Trial, sees correct lap arithmetic, races a compatible ghost and improves a best
+- J07 / local: Player starts before UTC midnight, finishes after it, uploads later and remains on the original challenge
+- J08 / local: New creator builds a closed circuit, corrects a gap, places gates and drives a valid lap
+- J09 / local: Creator tests against five AI, returns to exact editor context, undoes, reloads and recovers work
+- J10 / local: Creator exports, imports and gets identical gameplay meaning without executing hostile content
+- J11 / staged: Two owner editors conflict; stale editor preserves work and never overwrites the newer track
+- J12 / staged: Published track succeeds but catalog update conflicts; exact link works and listing retry is safe
+- J13 / local: Player downloads complete content, stops the server, opens a fresh browser document and races/edits offline
+- J14 / local: Existing release discovers a new version naturally and updates between runs without losing state
+- J15 / staged: Score submission times out after server acceptance; original ID reconciles once across two tabs
+- J16 / local: Graphics context is lost, phone rotates or input disconnects; invisible simulation stops and explicit resume works
+- J17 / local: Result/track invitation contains useful text and link; canceled share preserves state
+- J18 / local: Reduced-motion, muted and low-effects players can finish and read every transition/result
+- P01 / local: Draft storage
+- P02 / local: Result transaction
+- P03 / local: Outbox
+- P04 / staged: Owner authoring
+- P05 / staged: Public records
+- P06 / staged: Retention
+- P07 / staged: Native composition
+- P08 / staged: Record supported policy activation capability and preserve established public policies when no safe activation contract exists
+- P09 / local: Data-preserving release
+- M01 / local: Shared schemas, parser/serializer/compiler, independent geometric fixtures, one car and a loop; Clean source regeneration; round-trip integrity; swept collisions, skidpad/slalom/braking checks; input/pause/recovery state contracts
+- M02 / local: Six-car race, modular road editor, surface/prop/gate tools, real test drive, history and drafts; A new track can be built, validated, driven, recovered and exported/imported through the UI; one complete keyboard/touch-emulated journey
+- M03 / local: All 81 builds, twelve circuits, four cups, eight rivals, unlocks and results; Official tracks authored in Workshop; all references resolve; all tracks finish under seeded AI; seeded handling/pacing measurements complete
+- M04 / local: Saves, ghosts, daily definitions, offline pack, install/fullscreen, audio and sharing; Transaction/failure tests; genuine offline relaunch; natural update journey; phone layouts and keyboard focus
+- M05 / staged: Native composition, owner publication, discovery index, casual boards; Correct-host readback, ETag conflict and ambiguous-write recovery; supported public-policy activation where available, otherwise established-policy preservation, plus positive/negative record checks
+- M06 / live: Complete asset pack, required CI, audit evidence, release/rollback tools and browser verification; All required rows pass or have explicitly accepted scoped exceptions; exact package verified and previous-client update succeeds
+- C01 / local: Social artwork and complete initial OG/Twitter metadata
+- C02 / local: Favicon, raster, touch and maskable icon set
+- C03 / local: Complete asset sources, licenses, fonts and export inventory
+- C04 / staged: Required hosted CI refuses failed acceptance
+- C05 / local: Exact-source package and acceptance gate before every publication path
+- C06 / live: All required public assets and routes resolve after promotion
+- C07 / local: Credentials and private baselines absent from public package
+- C08 / local: Rollback preserves state and old-client dependencies
+- C09 / local: Reproducible browser evidence identifies exact tested environment
+- C10 / local: Fresh complete automated suite and accurate acceptance ledger
+- C11 / local: Pinned handbook 2.10 guidance and separate coverage/evidence decisions match the inventory and candidate
+- C12 / local: Required shared styles load consistently or produce recoverable startup failure through root and composed entry points
+- C13 / local: Every supported publisher refuses unresolved outcomes despite generic deployment instructions or agent-authored exception lists
+- C14 / staged: Publication phase journaling and operator recovery are exercised through the supported command after successful and ambiguous entry writes
+- R01 / local: Every home/menu action remains readable and reachable in phone portrait/landscape and enlarged text without horizontal clipping
